Z||000000||Monkeyman||06-30-2001||02:31 AM||||Cliff--Is UBB the same as YABB (Yet Another Bulletin Board)?  I also belong to a Suzuki Intruder forum which supports YABB.  They have some neat stuff you can do with posts (sub/super script, glowing letters, columns, etc).  Also, you can simply click on an icon and it takes care of the bracketed stuff so idiot users like myself don't have to keep referring to "UBB Code is ON".  If the two are the same, is it possible to simply activate these features?  Or is this much more involved?  To see what I'm referring to, please go <A HREF="http://www.intruderalert.com/" TARGET=_blank>here</A>.<P>I know you're very busy, but just wondered if this is possible and not time consuming.  <P>Thanx!<P>MM||||reg||5
Z||000001||isthiswhereiputausername?||06-30-2001||09:38 AM||||Nope..  they are different on the CGI.<P>There are plenty of UBB hacks out there to add all the extra features.  ones to add a whos online,private messaging,etc..<P>I have a lot of ubb hacks and scripts on a cd if you need any for this forum.<P><BR>||||reg||1
